  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "# Changelog\n\n## 0.5.1 (2026-11-16)\n\n- The package is licensed under MIT. The license text is in the `LICENSE` file at the package root.\n\n## 0.5.0 (2026-11-13)\n\n- Added `GetVariableInfo` to read the status variable and equipment constant definitions that IronGEM uses for S1F12 and S2F30 (name, unit, format, and for equipment constants min, max and default). Needs an IronGEM build with the `GEMGetVariableInfo` service.\n\n## 0.4.1 (2026-11-12)\n\n- First release on nuget.org.\n- The native gRPC libraries are now copied in projects that use `packages.config` too (the default of the Visual Studio .NET Framework templates). Before, `Initialize` returned 3 in those projects.\n- The package README is written for package users.\n\n## 0.4.0 (2026-11-09)\n\n- Added `SetMessageValidator` so the equipment application can accept, reject or reroute user-defined messages, both incoming and outgoing.\n- `GEMUserMsgReceived` handlers run on a separate sequential queue, so a long handler no longer stops the subscribe stream.\n- User message items carry their SECS format codes, and zero-length BIN items are allowed.\n\n## 0.3.0 (2026-11-05)\n\n- The connector keeps a copy of the equipment constants pushed by IronGEM: `GEMECVUpdated`, `TryGetECV`, `IsECVSynchronized`.\n- `SendUserMsg` returns the result reported by IronGEM.\n\n## 0.2.0 (2026-11-04)\n\n- Added `GetAlarmInfo` to read alarm definitions.\n\n## 0.1.5 (2026-11-02)\n\n- Added `SetEventEnable`, `GetEventEnable`, `SetAlarmEnable` and `GetAlarmEnable`.\n- `GetVariable` reports undefined VIDs and names.\n- After a reconnect, SECS is started again only when the application had called `Start`.\n- Fixed process program timeouts, the `Start`/`Stop` results and the default ACKC7.\n\n## 0.1.1 (2026-09-18)\n\n- Calls made before `Initialize` completes return `ERROR_CLIENT_INIT_FAILED` instead of `ERROR_GRPC_UNKNOWN`.\n\n## 0.1.0 (2026-07-22)\n\n- First release.",
